WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.091
Start with the domain
We want to solve this equation involving two logarithms. First determine the
domain, before changing the expression or calculating solutions.

2
00:00:12.091 --> 00:00:25.091
Domain, ]1, +∞[
Each logarithm's argument must be positive. Both x minus one and x plus one
must be positive, giving x greater than one.

3
00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:40.364
ln a + ln b = ln(ab)
On this domain, combine the logarithms into the logarithm of a product. The
product of x minus one and x plus one is a difference of squares.

4
00:00:40.364 --> 00:00:53.818
Use injectivity
Because the logarithm is strictly increasing, equal logarithms have equal
arguments. Thus x squared minus one equals three, and x squared equals four.

5
00:00:53.818 --> 00:01:07.727
Check the candidates
The algebraic equation gives two candidates, two and minus two. We are not
finished. Check each candidate against the conditions established at the
start.

6
00:01:07.727 --> 00:01:22.545
Verify and conclude
Minus two is not greater than one, so reject it. Two is admissible, and
substitution gives ln one plus ln three. The only solution is two.
